From 895fd5881093d377fadd2606f94665487e609bb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:19:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix OOB read of HE Capabilities optional field in
 get_max_nss_capability()

get_max_nss_capability() casts elems->he_capabilities to struct
ieee80211_he_capabilities * and, for bw == CHAN_WIDTH_160 or
CHAN_WIDTH_80P80, reads hecaps->optional[0..7] (the extended NSS/BW
support MCS maps) without checking elems->he_capabilities_len against
the length required for those fields.

The element parser (ieee802_11_parse_extension(), the
WLAN_EID_EXT_HE_CAPABILITIES case) only enforces
elen >= HE_CAPABILITIES_ELEM_MIN_LEN (21), which covers
he_mac_capab_info(6) + he_phy_capab_info(11) +
he_basic_supported_mcs_set(4) == 21 bytes; the optional[] trailer is
zero bytes by default and is only present if the sender included it.

bw is caller-supplied. wpas_parse_connection_info_link() in
wpa_supplicant/events.c derives it from the AP's own VHT/HE Operation
element in its (Re)Association Response frame via
get_sta_operation_chan_width()/get_operation_channel_width(), then
passes it straight into get_max_nss_capability(). A malicious or
corrupted AP that advertises a 160 MHz (or 80+80 MHz) HE/VHT Operation
element together with a minimum-length HE Capabilities element causes
wpa_supplicant to read up to 4 (or 8) bytes past the end of the HE
Capabilities element. If that element is at the end of the frame buffer,
this might read up to 8 bytes beyond the end of that buffer.

Only read the optional[] fields when he_capabilities_len is long enough
for the requested bandwidth; otherwise fall through to the VHT/HT
capability path as if no (usable) HE Capabilities element were present.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
(cherry picked from commit 895fd5881093d377fadd2606f94665487e609bb8)
---
 src/common/ieee802_11_common.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/common/ieee802_11_common.c b/src/common/ieee802_11_common.c
index 8ad201ef7..a906e3f93 100644
--- a/src/common/ieee802_11_common.c
+++ b/src/common/ieee802_11_common.c
@@ -3838,7 +3838,11 @@ unsigned int get_max_nss_capability(struct ieee802_11_elems *elems,
 		(struct ieee80211_he_capabilities *) elems->he_capabilities;
 	le16 mcs_map;
 
-	if (hecaps) {
+	if (hecaps &&
+	    (bw != CHAN_WIDTH_160 ||
+	     elems->he_capabilities_len >= HE_CAPABILITIES_ELEM_MIN_LEN + 4) &&
+	    (bw != CHAN_WIDTH_80P80 ||
+	     elems->he_capabilities_len >= HE_CAPABILITIES_ELEM_MIN_LEN + 8)) {
 		unsigned int max_nss_he;
 		const u8 *optional = hecaps->optional;
 
